      "writtenOn": "2026-09-10T17:54:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This allocates the memory through `vmalloc()`, which creates a mapping for the page in the kernel\u0027s vmalloc space, and that  mapping is unmapped when we free this. However, that is unnecessary. We can/should just grab the pages directly from the buddy allocator. Perhaps by using `alloc_page()` in `rust/kernel/page.rs` or add a `get_free_page()` invocation so we get a pointer to the page?",
      "revId": "627ecef83bfad9096784006ff893aa1c839da082",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0cba5ed2_f9f65bb5",
        "filename": "drivers/android/wrapfd/content.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 28,
      "author": {
        "id": 1014088
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-11T14:07:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I used to do this - I implemented a rust api for get_free_page() to stay similar to your original code, but due to some rust peculiarities (you cannot have a ref to something that\u0027s uninitialized memory) it became a rabbit hole. Alice suggested to use VVec of size PAGE_SIZE because it\u0027s guaranteed to be PAGE_SIZE aligned and therefore returns memory with sufficiently similar characteristics without requiring new rust APIs.",
      "parentUuid": "d181bf02_40c15a95",
      "revId": "627ecef83bfad9096784006ff893aa1c839da082",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "33d28771_e94781e8",
        "filename": "drivers/android/wrapfd/content.rs",
